; SETUP.MSG - the text Setup shows while it copies files.
;
; [disk1] is shown while Setup copies the files from Setup disk 1,
; [disk2] for disk 2, and so on up to [disk9].
;
; Write the text as a C string: in double quotes.  Strings that follow
; one another are joined into one.  Inside the quotes:
;
;   \r\n    a new line
;   \t      spaces up to the next tab stop (every 8 columns)
;   \\ \"   a backslash, a double quote
;   \xHH    the character with hex code HH (\x07 is a bullet)
;   \ooo    the character with octal code ooo
;
; Extended characters (code page 437) can also be typed as they are.
; The lines appear as written, centered as one block above the gauge.
; Up to 13 lines fit, and lines wider than 76 columns are broken at a
; space.  Lines that start with a semicolon are comments.

[disk1]
